  <!-- Spliced into jpackage's main.wxs by build-installer.sh, which also adds a
       reference to the property MSIRESTARTMANAGERCONTROL to the product. WiX 3
       syntax, like jpackage's own sources. -->
  <Fragment>
    <!-- Keeps Windows Installer from shutting down a running GROOVE when files of
         the installation are in use (in an upgrade, say). By default it offers to
         close the application through the Restart Manager, which fails for
         GROOVE: every launcher start is two processes, a windowless launcher and
         the JVM it starts as a child, and the Restart Manager cannot close the
         launcher, so its dialog reports failure and returns until both are gone.
         It would also end the Simulator's session rather than close its window,
         which most likely leaves no chance to ask about unsaved grammars.
         DisableShutdown still lets the Restart Manager find the processes that
         hold files, but not shut them down: Windows Installer then reports once
         that a reboot will be required, and on OK installs the new version next
         to the running one, whose files are moved aside and deleted at the next
         reboot. Disable, which falls back to Windows Installer's older FilesInUse
         dialog, is worse: that check matches loaded DLLs by name, so it takes
         minutes and lists every application that loads the same runtime DLLs as
         the bundled Java runtime (browsers, mail, IDEs), and Retry never clears. -->
    <Property Id="MSIRESTARTMANAGERCONTROL" Value="DisableShutdown"/>
  </Fragment>
